import{_ as a,C as n,o as s,c as d,a2 as o,E as r}from"./chunks/framework.CGSzHL4z.js";const b=JSON.parse('{"title":"Generators","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"features/generators.md","filePath":"features/generators.md","lastUpdated":1792713747000}'),i={name:"features/generators.md"};function l(h,e,g,c,p,u){const t=n("Screenshot");return s(),d("div",null,[e[0]||(e[0]=o('<h1 id="generators" tabindex="-1">Generators <a class="header-anchor" href="#generators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Generators&quot;">​</a></h1><p>A generator drives a value over a span of time on top of its keys. A camera keyed from A to B can shake while it travels, a light can flicker, a prop can spin, a colour can cycle. You set the generator&#39;s settings instead of keying every wobble, and the same Seed plays the same in Studio, in exports and in games.</p><h2 id="adding-one" tabindex="-1">Adding one <a class="header-anchor" href="#adding-one" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Adding one&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Right click an empty spot on a track&#39;s lane, or a channel&#39;s, and choose <strong>Add generator</strong>. A <strong>Generators</strong> lane appears right under that row, holding the new block. The block spans the keys selected on that row, or one second from where you clicked when none are. <strong>Add generator</strong> is also in a row header&#39;s menu (an actor row adds it on its root) and in the Inspector&#39;s property row menu.</p><p>A camera actor&#39;s row menu has <strong>Add camera shake</strong>: a Shake on its root with the Handheld preset. The <a href="./library#generators">Library&#39;s</a> Generators tab adds presets to the selected rows, or onto a row you drag them to.</p><h2 id="the-built-in-generators" tabindex="-1">The built-in generators <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-built-in-generators" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The built-in generators&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Generator</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Shake</strong>, <strong>Wiggle</strong></td><td>Seeded noise; Shake can die away with Decay</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Oscillate</strong></td><td>A regular wave</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Flicker / Strobe / Pulse</strong></td><td>Switches on/off values such as Enabled, or flickers a number</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Spin</strong></td><td>Turns continuously</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Recoil</strong></td><td>A kick and a bounce back, played once</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Overshoot / Settle</strong></td><td>A spring that follows the value under it, overshooting each change and settling</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Stepped</strong></td><td>Holds the value for 2, 3 or 4 frames at a time, for an on-twos look</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Hold / Fade</strong></td><td>Holds a number at its Value, easing in and out by the block&#39;s fades</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Cycle / Flipbook</strong></td><td>Steps through a list of values: enums, image ids, text</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Typewriter</strong></td><td>Types out a text, keeping rich text tags whole</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Generators drive numbers, vectors, UDim and UDim2 (a GUI&#39;s Position or Size), colours, NumberRanges, sequences, an actor&#39;s root and joints, and on/off values. One that can&#39;t drive a row is greyed in the menu with the reason.</p><h2 id="blocks-on-the-timeline" tabindex="-1">Blocks on the Timeline <a class="header-anchor" href="#blocks-on-the-timeline" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Blocks on the Timeline&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Blocks draw in magenta with the generator&#39;s icon, name and preset (&quot;Shake · Handheld&quot;). Drag to move (<code>Ctrl</code> copies), drag an edge to trim, and drag a top corner grip to fade in or out. Overlapping blocks stack in sub-lanes; lanes apply in order, sub-lanes top to bottom.</p><p>Right click a block for <strong>Blend</strong>, the fade shapes, <strong>Fit to playback range</strong>, <strong>Reseed</strong>, <strong>Save as preset...</strong>, <strong>Bake to keys</strong> (writes the result as a key every frame and removes the block), Duplicate and Delete.</p><p>Click a Generators lane&#39;s arrow to open its <strong>settings rows</strong>: one row per number setting and Influence, holding that setting&#39;s keys. They select, drag and nudge like any keys.</p><h2 id="the-generator-panel" tabindex="-1">The generator panel <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-generator-panel" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The generator panel&quot;">​</a></h2>',13)),r(t,{name:"feat-generator",caption:"A Shake generator on Rival's Head, selected. The Shape and Result preview at the top of the Inspector's generator panel redraws while Amplitude ramps up and down."}),r(t,{name:"feat-turret",caption:"Generators on a prop: the drone hovers on Oscillate with a little Wiggle on top, no keys needed. The turret beside it follows the walker with a Damped Track."}),e[1]||(e[1]=o('<p>Select a block and the Inspector shows its panel:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Section</th><th>Holds</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Preview</td><td>The block across its length with the playhead. <strong>Shape</strong> shows the generator alone, <strong>Result</strong> shows it applied on the keys</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Timing</strong></td><td>Start, Length, and Snap to Loop</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Target</strong></td><td>What it drives, which axes or channels, and Space (Local or World)</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Settings</strong></td><td>Amplitude, Frequency, Decay, Period and the rest, Seed with Reseed, and <strong>Vary each play</strong></td></tr><tr><td><strong>Blend</strong></td><td>Mode, Influence, Fade in and Fade out with their shapes</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Preset</strong></td><td>The generator&#39;s presets, and <strong>Save preset</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Each setting has a key diamond, so a shake can build up or calm down over the block.</p><h3 id="dragging-the-preview" tabindex="-1">Dragging the preview <a class="header-anchor" href="#dragging-the-preview" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Dragging the preview&quot;">​</a></h3><p>The preview is a control too. Drag up or down to change the size (Amplitude, Depth, Speed), left or right for the timing (Period, Frequency, Rate, Characters), or near a top corner for a fade. A click moves the playhead, and the wheel over a Shake or Wiggle steps its Seed. <strong>Shift+drag</strong> changes a second setting: Oscillate&#39;s Phase, a Strobe&#39;s Duty, a Shake&#39;s Decay, a Recoil&#39;s Kick and Bounce, a Typewriter&#39;s Delay. The preview&#39;s tooltip lists the drags for the generator you&#39;re on.</p><p>The scale is set when a block first shows and never refits, so a bigger Amplitude clips at the edges and a smaller one draws a smaller wave. <strong>Pin</strong> keeps the preview at the top while you scroll, and the window button opens a larger <strong>Generator</strong> window that follows the selected block.</p><h2 id="blend-modes" tabindex="-1">Blend modes <a class="header-anchor" href="#blend-modes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Blend modes&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Mode</th><th>Result</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><strong>Add</strong></td><td>The generator&#39;s offsets go on top of the keys</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Multiply</strong></td><td>Scales the keyed value (a flicker on a keyed brightness); Amplitude reads as a fraction</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Replace</strong></td><td>Takes over inside the block from the value at its start</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="drive-modes" tabindex="-1">Drive modes <a class="header-anchor" href="#drive-modes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Drive modes&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Some value types can be driven in more than one way. <strong>Drive</strong> in the Target section picks it:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>Modes beyond Around the value</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Colour</td><td><strong>Along a gradient</strong> (edited in the gradient editor) or <strong>HSV channels</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Number</td><td><strong>Between Low and High</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Position</td><td><strong>Orbit</strong> in a plane, as a circle or a figure 8</td></tr><tr><td>On/off</td><td><strong>Pattern</strong>, a grid of 1 to 32 steps you click</td></tr><tr><td>NumberRange</td><td><strong>Move</strong>, <strong>Spread</strong>, <strong>Between two ranges</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Sequence</td><td><strong>Move</strong>, <strong>Morph</strong> between two, <strong>Scroll</strong></td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="looping" tabindex="-1">Looping <a class="header-anchor" href="#looping" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Looping&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>Snap to Loop</strong> (in Timing) makes a Shake, Wiggle, Oscillate, Flicker, Spin or Cycle loop seamlessly. Its speed snaps to the nearest value where whole repeats fit the block: type a 1.1 s Period on a 3 s block and it becomes 1 s, three waves. The field always shows what plays. Right click the block &gt; <strong>Fit to playback range</strong> to put it over the loop region, or the whole scene.</p><h2 id="tips" tabindex="-1">Tips <a class="header-anchor" href="#tips" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Tips&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Clamp keeps colour channels between 0 and 1. Turn it off for lights and Highlights that take brighter than white, and leave it on for a Part&#39;s Color, which wraps round past 1.</li><li>A hue cycle on a grey or white shows nothing. Type <strong>S value</strong> 1 (and <strong>V value</strong> 1) to see it at full colour.</li><li>Custom generators are ModuleScripts tagged <code>AcesMotionGenerator</code>. <strong>New custom generator...</strong> in the Add generator menu makes a typed, commented template. <a href="./../extend/custom-generators">Custom generators</a> walks through writing one.</li><li>Keep a custom generator&#39;s <code>Offset</code> pure and use the <code>noise</code> it&#39;s given for randomness, so every player sees the same thing.</li></ul><h2 id="compared-to-roblox-s-animation-editor" tabindex="-1">Compared to Roblox&#39;s Animation Editor <a class="header-anchor" href="#compared-to-roblox-s-animation-editor" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Compared to Roblox&#39;s Animation Editor&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Roblox&#39;s Animation Editor has no procedural generators: a shake or a flicker there is keyed by hand, frame by frame, and only on a rig&#39;s joints. In AcesMotion a generator rides on top of the keys of any property, root or joint, and <strong>Bake to keys</strong> turns it into ordinary keys when you want to edit it by hand.</p>',17))])}const k=a(i,[["render",l]]);export{b as __pageData,k as default};
